<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - July 22.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - July 22.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF JULY 22 VERSUS JULY 15, 1997		     DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA   37/8     0/0     293/314   38/49   368/371    255</p>
<p> SASK.	9/1     0/0	97/102    4/5    110/108     63</p>
<p> B.C.	 2/1     0/0	27/24     5/7     34/32	17</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 1/1	4/4	5/5	  2</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 2/2	0/0	2/2	  1</p>
<p> TOTAL     48/10    0/0     420/443   51/65   519/518    338</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
